stay armed, they measure different axes (module SIZE and function\n68\tCOMPLEXITY), and the module-size ratchet is RE-BASED from raw physical lines to\n69\tSLOC. So this phase is **arm + re-base**, never arm + retire: nothing is deleted,\n70\tno pointer is moved. The plan's phase-2 draft\n71\t(`docs/plans/2026-08-29-complexity-sensor-plan.md#phase-2--arm-it-here-and-retire-whichever-sensor-the-ruling-retired`)\n72\tpredates the ruling and is written for 1a; the ruling governs where they differ.\n73\t\n74\t**Three acts, one direction.**\n75\t\n76\t1. **Arm (Q3 → 3a).** Add `[step:complexity]` to `docs/stack.ini`\n77\t   (`layer = product`, `from-stage = DevStg-Impl`) running\n78\t   `check_complexity.py --root . --mode enforce` — the exact-equality compare in\n79\t   both directions, nonzero on either. Growth fails (\"simplify, or take a reviewed\n80\t   baseline bump whose reason lands in the log\"); improvement fails (\"re-stamp\n81\t   downward in the same commit\"). No inline suppression pragma — the central\n82\t   baseline is the one escape hatch. Arming mints NO new spine row: `SR-183`\n83\t   already carries both postures in one contract (\"gated only where a repo opts\n84\t   in\"), and the opt-in IS the step's presence here. Report-only stays the shipped\n85\t   default; shipping downstream is phase 3, a separate WI.\n86\t\n87\t2. **Scope (Q2 → 2a).** The sensor censuses `tests/` as well as\n88\t   `project-trajectory/scripts/` — widened in `check_complexity.DEFAULT_INCLUDE`,\n89\t   the single home of this repo's census surface — and `docs/complexity-baseline`\n90\t   is re-stamped to seed the `tests/` functions over threshold. The line ratchet\n91\t   stays scripts-only, per the ruling. This closes WI-521's §3 sensor gap on the\n92\t   right axis instead of by extending the disputed line axis to a second tree.\n93\t\n94\t3. **Re-base (Q1 → 1c).** `tests/test_module_size_ratchet.py` re-bases from raw\n95\t   physical lines to **SLOC** (non-blank, non-comme