{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0141MpW7Tx4fcQgPsBhHTyzM","type":"tool_result","content":"<system-reminder>[Truncated: PARTIAL view — showing lines 1-862 of 1555 total (38323 tokens, cap 25000). Call Read with offset=863 limit=862 for the next page, or Grep to find a specific section. Do NOT answer from this page alone if the answer may be further in the file.]</system-reminder>\n\n1\t<!-- Copied verbatim on 2026-08-30 from C:/Projects/ai-template-plans/complexity-pushback/PLAN.md — the plan of record for the rows that cite it; its companions there (the source reports, the prototype, the drafts, the review transcripts) stay outside the repo. -->\n2\t\n3\t# complexity-pushback — repo-integration plan\n4\t\n5\t**Status:** plan only. Nothing in `C:\\Projects\\ai-template` was modified writing this.\n6\t**Written:** 2026-08-29. **Read at:** `ai-template` HEAD `85fb3742` (branch `contract_split`).\n7\t**Working tree at survey time was dirty in four paths** — `PROJECT_STATE.html`,\n8\t`docs/decisions-for-review-2026-08-29-slices-4-6.md`, `docs/stage`, `docs/status.md`,\n9\tplus an untracked `docs/log.d/2026-08-29-owner-rulings-oi67-decisions.md`. Everything quoted\n10\tbelow was read from the working tree EXCEPT `docs/status.md`, which was read at HEAD via\n11\t`git show HEAD:docs/status.md`. A session executing this plan must re-read those five paths\n12\tbefore touching them: another session was mid-OI-67-slice-6 the whole time.\n13\t\n14\t**Re-verified after the concurrent session committed.** While this plan was being written the\n15\ttree advanced to `b19d4bf7` (\"sitting: the owner accepts decisions 4.1, 6.2, 6.7 and 6.8 of the\n16\tOI-67 slices — recorded, nothing changes in code\") and went clean. That commit touched only\n17\t`PROJECT_STATE.html`, `docs/stage`, `docs/status.md`, `docs/decisions-for-review-2026-08-29-slices-4-6.md`\n18\tand a new log fragment — none of which this plan quotes normatively. **Every load-bearing\n19\tnumber below was re-measured at `b19d4bf7` and is unchanged:** the watermark still reads\n20\t`IF=173 LLR=205 OI=67 SR=182 TC=201 WI=534`, and `wc -c` still gives `PROCESS.md` 87,836 ·\n21\t`PROCESS_OPTIONS.md` 179,209 · `AGENTS.template.md` 9,980 · `byte-budget-guard/SKILL.md` 4,795.\n22\t\n23\t**Sources this plan executes:** `..\\knowledge-pack-review\\00-SYNTHESIS.md` §2, §3 ranks 1–3,\n24\t§5 plan 1; `..\\knowledge-pack-review\\05-compact-code-and-complexity-pushback.md` §2, §4\n25\t(P1/P2/P3/P4/P6), §5. **The owner has approved the proposal in principle**; phase 0 is the\n26\truling that decides its shape, not its existence.\n27\t\n28\t**The script itself is not in this plan.** A sibling agent is prototyping it under\n29\t`prototype/` — it now exists (`prototype/check_complexity.py`, 49 tests green, census in\n30\t`prototype/analysis.txt` and `prototype/PROTOTYPE-NOTES.md`; see `README.md` beside this file).\n31\tThe prototype's numbers are the WORKING figures in this plan and the OI brief. Do not copy a\n32\tnumber out of report 05 into a registry cell or a baseline file: report 05's figures were taken\n33\twith an unvalidated walker and read materially high (`plan_round.record` 135 there, 61 by the\n34\tvalidated prototype). The shipped script's own first run is the only number that may be stamped\n35\tinto the repo; the prototype's are what the ruling is read against.\n36\t\n37\t---\n38\t\n39\t## 0. What the program is, in one paragraph\n40\t\n41\tBuild `check_complexity.py` — a stdlib-`ast` Sonar-style **cognitive complexity** + SLOC\n42\tcensus per function (plus a reported, ungated public-symbol count per module), with a central\n43\tTSV baseline, exact equality in both directions, `--report` / `--restamp`, and **no inline\n44\tsuppression pragma ever**. Ship it `--report`-only; arming it is an opt-in\n45\t`PROCESS_OPTIONS.md` layer. Land it **as a trade, not an addition**: the same ruling that\n46\tadmits it decides whether `tests/test_module_size_ratchet.py` retires, which is the owner\n47\tquestion already banked in the 2026-08-20 log. Alongside it: a `deep-module-design`\n48\t`scope: kit` skill (the one real content gap), and one PROCESS.md §3 bullet formalising the\n49\tstructure-vs-behaviour commit split that WI-521 slices 1–2 already practised.\n50\t\n51\t**Two rulings constrain everything here and neither is reopened.** **D-7** (2026-08-10) tore\n52\tdown the *gating* duplication census; any proposal that re-arms a duplication gate is dead on\n53\tarrival, and this program adds no duplication check of any kind. **OI-16** (owner correction,\n54\t2026-08-12) is the program's warrant: *\"the monolith risk was really around function size /\n55\tcomplexity, not strictly file size.\"*\n56\t\n57\t---\n58\t\n59\t## 1. The seams, exactly as they are today\n60\t\n61\tEach subsection records what the repo does **now**, with the file path and a verbatim\n62\tpattern. This is the reference the execution WIs work from; nothing here is a proposal.\n63\t\n64\t### 1.1 OI filing — `docs/requirements/open-items.toml`\n65\t\n66\t**Carrier.** One TOML table per decision, id-keyed and bare: `[open_item.OI-###]`. The file's\n67\town header states the contract (it declares `IF-073`):\n68\t\n69\t```\n70\t# Contract IF-073: one `[open_item.OI-###]` table per owner decision, carrying\n71\t#     `title`, `status`, `raised`, `one_line`, `decision`, `blast_radius`,\n72\t#     `options`, `recommendation` and `wi_refs`. `status` is `pending` or\n73\t#     `ruled`, and only a pending row renders as a brief card — a ruled row is\n74\t#     history, and the Decisions log is its record. `-000` example rows are\n75\t#     dropped, and an absent registry renders an empty queue rather than\n76\t#     failing, so a repo carrying no decisions still has the surface.\n77\t```\n78\t\n79\t**The `-000` row IS the schema** (`docs/requirements/open-items.toml` lines 16–27), and its\n80\tcell values are the authoring guidance. Copied verbatim as the pattern to fill:\n81\t\n82\t```toml\n83\t[open_item.OI-000]\n84\ttitle = \"Example row - the shape of an owner decision brief\"\n85\tstatus = \"pending\"\n86\traised = \"2026-01-01\"\n87\tone_line = \"\"\"the one-line form status.md projects - what is being decided, and the recommendation in a clause\"\"\"\n88\tdecision = \"\"\"What is being decided, who raised it and when, and any context a ruler needs that is not obvious from the one-line.\"\"\"\n89\tblast_radius = \"\"\"What breaks or changes if this is ruled either way - the honest cost, not the optimistic one.\"\"\"\n90\toptions = \"\"\"Option (a) ... · Option (b) ... · Option (c) ... - each with its FOR and AGAINST, separated by the middot the other registries use for lists-in-cells.\"\"\"\n91\trecommendation = \"The driver's recommendation and WHY, in the same voice a reviewer would argue it.\"\n92\twi_refs = [\"WI-000\"]\n93\t```\n94\t\n95\t**Field census over the 59 real rows** (`grep -oE '^[a-z_]+ = ' | sort | uniq -c`):\n96\t`title`/`status`/`recommendation`/`raised`/`options`/`one_line` on all 59; `ruling_ref` and\n97\t`ruled_date` on 58; `blast_radius` on 57; `decision` on 49; `wi_refs` on 26. So\n98\t`blast_radius` and `decision` are conventionally-required-but-not-schema-required, and\n99\t`wi_refs` is genuinely optional — **a brief may be filed with no WI row yet**, which is what\n100\tphase 0 does.\n101\t\n102\t**How the fields actually work, read from live rows.**\n103\t\n104\t- `status` — `pending` while it owes a ruling, flipped to `ruled` when the owner answers.\n105\t  Only a `pending` row renders as a card. **There is exactly one `status = \"pending\"` row in\n106\t  the file today and it is `OI-000`, the example** — every real OI is ruled. So the phase-0\n107\t  brief will be the only live card, which is the surface the owner reads.\n108\t- `raised` — the date the question was put, `YYYY-MM-DD`.\n109\t- `wi_refs` — `[\"WI-###\"]`, the rows that carry the work. Filled after the ruling for a\n110\t  brief filed before any WI exists.\n111\t- `one_line` — what `docs/status.md` projects. **The house convention on a ruled row is to\n112\t  PREPEND the ruling and keep the original one-line behind it**, e.g. OI-67:\n113\t  `\"\"\"RULED (a) 2026-08-29 — the owner: \"...\" Original brief: rule the shape of an interface row; recommend (a): ...\"\"\"`\n114\t- `decision` — what is being decided plus the context a ruler needs. On a ruled row the\n115\t  ruling is written INTO this cell at the top (OI-16 opens `RULED ADDENDUM (owner,\n116\t  2026-08-13): ...`).\n117\t- `ruled_date` + `ruling_ref` — added at the ruling. `ruling_ref` points at\n118\t  `docs/log.md#decisions-log`, `docs/repo-lock.md#d-5`, or a\n119\t  `docs/log.d/<date>-<slug>.md` fragment (OI-67 uses\n120\t  `docs/log.d/2026-08-29-oi67-ruled-a.md`).\n121\t- `options` — lettered, each with FOR and AGAINST. Long rows use `###`-headed markdown\n122\t  inside the `\"\"\"` string (OI-67 does); short rows use one `·`-separated line (OI-11 does).\n123\t- `recommendation` — the driver's call and why, argued in a reviewer's voice.\n124\t\n125\t**How the brief is composed and rendered.** There is no composer script — the brief is\n126\t**hand-authored into the TOML row**, and `project-trajectory/scripts/gen_open_items.py`\n127\tRENDERS it. That module's docstring is explicit about owning no second opinion:\n128\t\n129\t> ANTI-DUPLICATION, deliberately: the git archaeology and the cell comparison live in\n130\t> `trace.reattest_model`, and the pending projection lives in `pending.pending_block`. This\n131\t> module imports both and RENDERS.\n132\t\n133\tIt emits three ordered sections into `docs/open-items.html`: (1) one card per\n134\t`status=pending` row (the one-line, what is being decided, blast radius, options,\n135\trecommendation, and the WI rows that carry the work); (2) approval & re-attestation, every\n136\t`Drafted`-or-drifted SR with its whole chain; (3) pending owner actions, reused verbatim from\n137\t`pending.pending_block`.\n138\t\n139\t**Regen command** (`--root` defaults to cwd, `--check` byte-compares for the freshness gate;\n140\tthe step name is `open-items` in `check.py` and the `[generated]` row is\n141\t`docs/open-items.html = openitems`):\n142\t\n143\t```\n144\tpython project-trajectory/scripts/gen_open_items.py --root .\n145\tpython project-trajectory/scripts/
